# NO MERGE DRIVER ON THE APPEND-ONLY STORES. This is deliberate. Do not add `merge=union` back.
#
# WHY (2026-07-24, found while repairing the fourth duplication). These files previously carried:
#
#     data/games.ladder.jsonl merge=union
#     data/games.bo3.jsonl    merge=union
#     *.jsonl                 merge=union
#
# with the comment "readers dedupe by id, so duplicate lines are harmless". Both halves of that
# were wrong, and the union driver — not `git merge -X ours` — is the mechanism that duplicated
# the store (7,040 lines once, then 401, then 8,139).
#
# `merge=union` resolves a conflicting hunk by concatenating BOTH sides in full. On an append-only
# log, every divergent reconciliation therefore replays the whole appended block, doubling it.
# The critical consequence: **the union driver applies to `git rebase` as well as `git merge`.**
# Switching push-all.bat from `merge -X ours` to `rebase` does NOT stop this by itself. The driver
# had to go, or the duplication returns on the next divergence.
#
# And the duplicates are not harmless. They break the S7 store-shape assertions in
# engine/sanity_check.py, and they corrupt every game count the site and the white paper publish.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS NOW INSTEAD. With no driver, two writers appending to the same tail produce a real
# merge conflict and the reconciliation STOPS. That is the intended behaviour, and it matches
# push-all.bat, which refuses to auto-resolve. A conflict here is a loud, recoverable event;
# a silent doubling is neither.
#
# TO RESOLVE ONE. Keep both sides' lines, then let the deduplicator settle it:
#
#     git checkout --theirs data/games.ladder.jsonl   # or edit to keep both blocks
#     python engine/dedupe_store.py --write           # idempotent, order-preserving, atomic
#     git add data/games.ladder.jsonl
#
# The ingest itself never creates duplicates: engine/durable-ingest.js reads every existing id
# before appending. Duplicates have only ever entered this repository through git reconciliation.

# THE GAME STORES ARE SETS, NOT TEXT. One line per game, keyed on game id, append-only. Git's line
# merge is meaningless on them and its default resolutions are destructive: taking either side of a
# conflict deletes whatever the other side collected, and the replays behind those games age off
# Showdown's server, so the loss is permanent and invisible. build/merge-jsonl-store.js unions them
# by id instead. Bind it once per clone with: bash build/setup-git.sh
data/games.ladder.jsonl           merge=jsonl-store
data/games.bo3.jsonl              merge=jsonl-store
data/games.ots.jsonl              merge=jsonl-store
data/games.ladder.raw-logs.jsonl  merge=jsonl-store
data/games.bo3.raw-logs.jsonl     merge=jsonl-store

# ── A LINE ENDING BLANKED THE GATE TWICE IN THREE DAYS. THESE FILES ARE NOT TRANSLATED. ──────────
#
# `engine/engine_release.js` freezes 26 files as "the engine" and identifies a release by the
# sha256 of their BYTES. `core.autocrlf` is `true` on the working machine, so any file git considers
# text is rewritten to CRLF on checkout. That makes the release id depend on whether git last
# touched the file or its generator did — not on anything about the simulator.
#
# It has fired twice. 2026-08-26: `data/tags.json` went 794,538 -> 836,962 bytes on a rebase and the
# engine was re-cut under a new id with no code change. 2026-08-28 09:58Z->10:06Z: the same file,
# the same way, and the gate fell from 7 of 8 clauses PASS to 5 of 8 because the roster, whole-game
# and staged-mechanics artifacts all stamp a release the tree no longer is. Measured on that tree:
# the release's own copy and the working copy were raw-unequal, CRLF-normalised EQUAL and JSON
# deep-equal. `docs/ENGINE.md` predicted the second occurrence in writing and prose did not stop it.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the CHECKED-OUT bytes to LF and overrides core.autocrlf, so a checkout now
# reproduces exactly what the generator wrote. Every one of these blobs is already LF in the index
# and already LF in the working tree, so adding the attribute moves no byte today; it removes the
# translation that would move them tomorrow. Demonstrated RED before it was added: writing the
# committed blob and then `git checkout HEAD -- data/tags.json` took the digest 576a4bbe91af ->
# a32ee545cf67 with nothing edited.
#
# THIS IS NOT A MERGE ATTRIBUTE AND MUST NOT BECOME ONE. See the block at the top of this file:
# `merge=union` duplicated the store four times and is permanently banned. `eol` is unrelated to
# conflict resolution and changes no merge behaviour.
#
# The list is the frozen SOURCES set, so read it against `engine/engine_release.js`. Nine sources
# are deliberately ABSENT — medicham2-browser.js, rollout_leaf.js, position_features.js,
# engine/tags.js, mc_key.js, set_priors.js, smogon_priors.js, data/quality-filter.json and
# data/engine-data.js are CRLF in the working tree today. Pinning those to LF would rewrite them,
# move every release id, and break `tests/roster.js`, whose red demonstrations match `\r\n` against
# the simulator's source. That is a separate, larger job and it is filed, not done here.
engine/board.js                  text eol=lf
engine/champions_sim.js          text eol=lf
engine/lookup.js                 text eol=lf
engine/quality.js                text eol=lf
engine/showdown_path.js          text eol=lf
engine/pp.js                     text eol=lf
data/tags.json                   text eol=lf
data/abra-tags.js                text eol=lf
data/residual-order.json         text eol=lf
data/switchin-order.json         text eol=lf
data/move-effects.js             text eol=lf
data/ability-blocks.json         text eol=lf
data/smogon-priors.json          text eol=lf
data/move-priors.json            text eol=lf
data/regulations.json            text eol=lf
data/policy-weights.json         text eol=lf
data/policy-weights-joint.json   text eol=lf
data/rollout-switch-census.json  text eol=lf

# ── A TRACKED RELEASE SNAPSHOT IS BYTES, NOT TEXT. 2026-09-09, MEASURE. ───────────────────────────
#
# data/releases/<id>/ is a COPY of the frozen sources, and release.json holds the sha256 of the RAW
# bytes of each copy at cut time — the id is the digest of those digests. Nine of the sources are
# deliberately unpinned above and are CRLF in this working tree, so a release holds a MIX: 18 LF
# files and 9 CRLF files, and open() refuses the release if a single byte of either moves.
#
# Measured 2026-09-09: b730e44f3314 was staged with `git add -f` (its 29 files carried no attribute,
# so core.autocrlf normalised them to LF in the index) and the next checkout of those paths wrote
# CRLF back over ALL of them. open() then refused it — engine/board.js: manifest c85a3b756c98,
# snapshot 2e9c917b8e82, the CRLF form — and every gate artifact stamped against it went dark.
#
# `-text`, NOT `text eol=lf`. eol=lf would normalise the nine CRLF-at-cut files to LF on every
# checkout and clone, so their digests would never again match the manifest and every release
# holding them would be unopenable on every machine. `-text` switches conversion OFF in both
# directions: the index stores exactly the bytes on disk and a checkout writes exactly the index.
# It changes no release id, because release.json is not rewritten. Diff still works (-text is not
# `binary`, which is `-text -diff`). NOT a merge attribute; see the top of this file.
data/releases/**                 -text

# ── THE THIRD OCCURRENCE, AND THIS ONE REACHED COMPARABILITY. 2026-09-08, MEASURE. ───────────────
#
# The block above pins the ENGINE's frozen sources. It does not pin the INSTRUMENT that measures
# them, and on 2026-09-08 that gap moved two digests with nothing edited:
#
#   data/protocol-events.json   7c9de3868d6f -> 2638eb253525   (`git status` reports it CLEAN)
#   engine/medicham2-browser.js 9a54ee6881cf -> 8bdea30dbb42   (CR-insensitive diff of ZERO lines)
#
# `data/protocol-events.json` is `steering.alignment_inputs` — the DECLARED SKIP LIST that decides
# which Showdown lines may count as a divergence — and `engine/arms_comparable.js` compares it
# UNCONDITIONALLY. So two runs with a BYTE-IDENTICAL skip list were one checkout away from being
# called NOT COMPARABLE. A false refusal is not the safe direction: it is how a checker becomes the
# thing people route around, which this repository has already paid for as "one of the two known
# failures".
#
# THE SET BELOW IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN. It is every file whose CONTENT DIGEST decides a
# comparability question and is not already pinned: `steering.driver_code`'s static require closure
# of engine/game_differential.js, the alignment rule and the rule that derives it, the census that
# selects the sample, and the artifact directory those runs are pinned to and compared against.
# Re-derive it rather than trusting this list — a typed list is the ban list of four in a costume.
#
# THE NINE SOURCES NAMED ABOVE ARE STILL ABSENT and this block does not change that; pinning them
# still moves every release id and still breaks `tests/roster.js`. That is why the digest fix is at
# the READ as well: `engine_release.sha12Content` makes the comparability digests EOL-insensitive on
# a machine that ALREADY holds the wrong bytes, which an attribute cannot do — an attribute only
# fixes the next checkout. The two halves cover different populations and both are needed.
#
# Every blob below is pure LF in the index today with ZERO lone CRs, measured before adding this, so
# these attributes move no byte now. They remove the translation that would move them tomorrow.
